# Actuator Research Tool

- App lives in `actuator-research/`: FastAPI backend (`backend/`), vanilla JS frontend (`frontend/`), pytest suite (`tests/`).
- Units: linear ratings in N and mm/s, rotary in N·m and rpm; sizing math is SI internally (`backend/sizing.py`).
- Quality gate: `bash actuator-research/scripts/check.sh` (ruff, `node --check`, pytest). Run it before every commit; stage explicit paths (never `git add -A`). Commit and push to `origin` after each coherent unit of work.
- Dev server: `bash actuator-research/scripts/dev.sh` on **http://127.0.0.1:8001/** (port 8000 belongs to the Fastener Analysis Tool). `--reload` picks up edits; verify UI changes in Cursor's Simple Browser (task **Actuator Research: Open in Cursor Browser**).
- User data (added actuators, notes) lives in `actuator-research/backend/data/user/` (gitignored). Tests isolate it with `ACTUATOR_DATA_DIR`.

## Catalog data and IP

- `backend/data/catalog_seed.json` holds **illustrative placeholders only**. Real entries need a `source` (datasheet title, revision, page) and an official manufacturer `datasheet_url`.
- Record only the specification numbers needed; never commit vendor datasheet PDFs, copied catalog pages, or long verbatim text. Do not link to unauthorized redistributions.
